{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-643bfb8e-56aa-45dc-8d95-0c27d2d72d16","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-90736b2fade10022","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-9gqorxo_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E002.md","content":"# Llama Stack API stability guarantees and GA hardening\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the API stability guarantee that GA requires for Llama\nStack: versioned APIs, an enforced deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade\npath from the last two Tech Preview releases. It also remediates the quality\ngaps (scale limits, error handling, and other GA-bar gaps) identified by the\nGA-readiness assessment, closing the quality deficit that Tech Preview\nstatus currently excuses.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Introduce API versioning across the published Llama Stack surface\n  (LlamaStackDistribution CRD and the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs).\n- Implement the deprecation policy mechanism: deprecated surface is\n  identified, communicated, and retained for the documented grace period.\n- Build and automate upgrade-path testing covering migration from the last\n  two Tech Preview releases to the GA release.\n- Remediate the GA-bar quality gaps recorded in the GA-readiness assessment\n  (expected to include scale limits and error handling/failure-mode\n  coverage); each remediation follows the assessment's recommendation unless\n  a documented decision defers it with rationale.\n- Update in-repo references (examples, captions, doc pointers) that fall out\n  of these changes — incidental touch-ups only; the GA documentation uplift\n  is handled separately.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The published API surface carries explicit version identifiers, and the\n  versioning scheme is documented.\n- The deprecation policy is documented and mechanically enforced: use of\n  deprecated surface produces the documented warning/behavior during the\n  grace period.\n- An automated upgrade-path test migrates a distribution from each of the\n  last two Tech Preview releases to the GA release and passes.\n- Every gap item in the ratified GA scope that falls in this epic's areas\n  (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling) is either\n  remediated or explicitly deferred with a recorded rationale accepted by\n  stakeholders.\n- All changes merge through a green Konflux build pipeline for the\n  llama-stack midstream repo.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee —\n  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the\n  last two TP releases. This epic is the direct deliverer of HLR-2.\n- Assessment-driven gap remediation (the actionable output of HLR-1) is\n  bundled here: it edits the same API/quality surface of the same component\n  and team as the stability work, so it is not a separately schedulable\n  deliverable.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36083,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a386f0d292bde4de","agent_id":"a56f9ec584c0a068d","session_id":"bc08d67b-4a0e-4de8-9000-b947c2646aca","uuid":"f4ed52da-da1c-47a8-b50e-7766b7d9e4d3","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:39:27.019Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
