licy mechanism: deprecated surface is\n51\t  identified, communicated, and retained for the documented grace period.\n52\t- Build and automate upgrade-path testing covering migration from the last\n53\t  two Tech Preview releases to the GA release.\n54\t- Remediate the GA-bar quality gaps recorded in the GA-readiness assessment\n55\t  (expected to include scale limits and error handling/failure-mode\n56\t  coverage); each remediation follows the assessment's recommendation unless\n57\t  a documented decision defers it with rationale.\n58\t- Update in-repo references (examples, captions, doc pointers) that fall out\n59\t  of these changes — incidental touch-ups only; the GA documentation uplift\n60\t  is handled separately.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- The published API surface carries explicit version identifiers, and the\n65\t  versioning scheme is documented.\n66\t- The deprecation policy is documented and mechanically enforced: use of\n67\t  deprecated surface produces the documented warning/behavior during the\n68\t  grace period.\n69\t- An automated upgrade-path test migrates a distribution from each of the\n70\t  last two Tech Preview releases to the GA release and passes.\n71\t- Every gap item in the ratified GA scope that falls in this epic's areas\n72\t  (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling) is either\n73\t  remediated or explicitly deferred with a recorded rationale accepted by\n74\t  stakeholders.\n75\t- All changes merge through a green Konflux build pipeline for the\n76\t  llama-stack midstream repo.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee —\n81\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the\n82\t  last two TP releases. This epic is the direct deliverer of HLR-2.\n83\t- Assessment-driven gap remediation (the actionable output of HLR-1) is\n84\t  bundled here: it edits the same API/quality surface of the same component\n85\t  and team as the stability work, so it is not a separately schedulable\n86\t  deliverable.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9399e9c72dcd92ec","agent_id":"a92d6397dd8e68ae4","session_id":"bc08d67b-4a0e-4de8-9000-b947c2646aca","uuid":"e963a07b-4007-4b67-8df2-1567e5a0a203","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:42:27.747Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d1f16b73e62732f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
