tent process; E002, E004, and E005\n128\t(the code epics) each carry the Rule 25 Konflux build-pipeline-green AC. No\n129\texternally-controlled preconditions are misfiled as ACs — the\n130\tstakeholder-review ACs on E001/E003 condition the epic's own deliverable\n131\t(the ratified scope / accepted posture documents), not access granted by\n132\toutside parties. No sibling draft-ID references (\"E001\" etc.) appear in any\n133\tepic body; cross-epic references use descriptive phrasing (\"the Llama Stack\n134\tstability work\").\n135\t\n136\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n137\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: TP feedback consolidation from support\n138\ttickets (E001 scope + AC), quality-gap remediation bounded to GA-bar gaps\n139\t(E002, with the out-of-scope boundary — no new feature development —\n140\texplicitly respected and noted in Health Warnings), support posture (E003),\n141\tguardrails promotion (E004), Dashboard default-on (E005), and documentation\n142\tuplift including TP migration notes (E006). The strategy's single open\n143\tquestion (GA scope size) is carried forward as the E001 investigation gate\n144\trather than dropped. Missing strategy sections (Impacted Teams, Dependencies\n145\ttable, Given/When/Then ACs, NFRs) are flagged in Health Warnings with the\n146\tderivation approach stated. Downstream coverage is complete: E001's four gap\n147\tareas are all picked up by E002's remediation scope and AC. The strategy has\n148\tno Prerequisites & Process Gates section declaring documentation support, but\n149\tHLR-6 makes docs a requirement and E006 delivers it, so Rule 11 is satisfied.\n150\tNo conditional branches are needed — the one unknown (GA scope) is a\n151\tmagnitude unknown handled by a gate, not a bounded-outcome branch.\n152\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82b3adab700edd23","agent_id":"a427fa9988392833b","session_id":"bc08d67b-4a0e-4de8-9000-b947c2646aca","uuid":"d33c9414-12f8-48c4-9419-f69bea1cdee8","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:4