{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8dfba2f0636e31","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: TrustyAI guardrails as a supported Llama Stack integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# TrustyAI guardrails as a supported Llama Stack integration\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic promotes safety guardrails via TrustyAI from an experimental flag\n35\tto a supported, documented integration for GA Llama Stack distributions.\n36\tEnterprise customers building production GenAI applications on the GA\n37\tdistribution need guardrails as a first-class supported capability, validated\n38\tagainst the versioned GA API surface.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Remove the experimental/opt-in flag gating the TrustyAI guardrails\n43\t  integration so it ships as a standard supported capability of GA\n44\t  distributions.\n45\t- Harden and validate the integration against the versioned GA API surface\n46\t  and deprecation policy delivered by the Llama Stack stability work,\n47\t  including its behavior across the supported configuration matrix.\n48\t- Author the integration documentation (configuration, supported deployment\n49\t  topologies, operational guidance) marking it as supported — this is\n50\t  integration-specific documentation that belongs to this epic's deliverable,\n51\t  distinct from the platform-wide GA documentation uplift.\n52\t- Add/extend validation coverage for the integration in the TrustyAI\n53\t  operator and integration test suites.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The TrustyAI guardrails integration is available in GA Llama Stack\n58\t  distributions without any experimental opt-in flag.\n59\t- The integration is validated against the versioned GA API surface and the\n60\t  validation passes as part of the integration test suite.\n61\t- Integration documentation is published describing configuration and\n62\t  supported topologies, marked as a supported (not experimental) capability.\n63\t- All changes merge through a green Konflux build pipeline for the TrustyAI\n64\t  midstream repo.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n69\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. This epic is\n70\t  the direct deliverer of HLR-4.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82b3adab700edd23","agent_id":"a427fa9988392833b","session_id":"bc08d67b-4a0e-4de8-9000-b947c2646aca","uuid":"6fa98694-b6a9-4a26-add6-7c16f50e5098","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:46:44.164Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8dfba2f0636e31","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
