{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6d87c4acc5d5b4c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: no systematic GA-readiness\n30\tassessment of Llama Stack has been done, and the full inventory of gaps\n31\tbetween current Tech Preview quality and the GA bar is not known. This\n32\tinvestigation produces the definitive GA scope — a prioritized, sized\n33\tinventory of quality gaps across API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits,\n34\tand error handling — that determines the scope of the downstream stability,\n35\thardening, and support-posture work.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Audit the published Llama Stack API surface (LlamaStackDistribution CRD and\n40\t  the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs) against GA stability requirements,\n41\t  identifying unstable or undocumented surface area.\n42\t- Evaluate the upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases,\n43\t  identifying breakage and missing migration coverage.\n44\t- Assess scale limits (concurrent distributions, request throughput, provider\n45\t  saturation) against enterprise production expectations, using TP feedback\n46\t  scattered across support tickets as an input.\n47\t- Review error handling and failure modes across the distribution's\n48\t  components (inference provider, storage, operator reconciliation).\n49\t- Consolidate TP feedback from support tickets into structured findings.\n50\t- Produce the GA scope document: a prioritized gap inventory with severity,\n51\t  remediation recommendation, and rough sizing per gap, ratifying what is in\n52\t  and out of the GA bar.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- An assessment report exists covering all four gap areas (API stability,\n57\t  upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with each finding classified\n58\t  by severity and including a remediation recommendation and rough sizing.\n59\t- TP feedback from support tickets has been consolidated into the report's\n60\t  findings, with no known TP feedback source left unreviewed.\n61\t- A GA scope document is produced that enumerates the gaps that must close\n62\t  for GA and explicitly defers gaps that fall outside the GA bar, and it has\n63\t  been reviewed with product and engineering stakeholders.\n64\t- The gap inventory is sufficient for the downstream stability and hardening\n65\t  work, and for the support-posture work, to be scoped without re-deriving\n66\t  the analysis.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between\n71\t  current TP quality and the GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale\n72\t  limits, error handling), producing the definitive GA scope. This epic is\n73\t  the direct deliverer of HLR-1.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83473cf1cf19135a","agent_id":"a0e56b6a1c5c0aca8","session_id":"bc08d67b-4a0e-4de8-9000-b947c2646aca","uuid":"0ed5577e-0881-486e-a7e8-dd27d4c9da8b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:48:59.519Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6d87c4acc5d5b4c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
