{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99cc94b22bc04e7d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantees and GA hardening\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds the gap inventory materially\n15\t    larger or smaller than assumed, re-scope this epic's remediation items to the\n16\t    ratified GA scope; if volume exceeds a sprint, split remediation into follow-on\n17\t    hardening epics rather than growing this epic unboundedly.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack API stability guarantees and GA hardening\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic delivers the API stability guarantee that GA requires for Llama\n40\tStack: versioned APIs, an enforced deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade\n41\tpath from the last two Tech Preview releases. It also remediates the quality\n42\tgaps (scale limits, error handling, and other GA-bar gaps) identified by the\n43\tGA-readiness assessment, closing the quality deficit that Tech Preview\n44\tstatus currently excuses.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Introduce API versioning across the published Llama Stack surface\n49\t  (LlamaStackDistribution CRD and the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs).\n50\t- Implement the deprecation policy mechanism: deprecated surface is\n51\t  identified, communicated, and retained for the documented grace period.\n52\t- Build and automate upgrade-path testing covering migration from the last\n53\t  two Tech Preview releases to the GA release.\n54\t- Remediate the GA-bar quality gaps recorded in the GA-readiness assessment\n55\t  (expected to include scale limits and error handling/failure-mode\n56\t  coverage); each remediation follows the assessment's recommendation unless\n57\t  a documented decision defers it with rationale.\n58\t- Update in-repo references (examples, captions, doc pointers) that fall out\n59\t  of these changes — incidental touch-ups only; the GA documentation uplift\n60\t  is handled separately.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- The published API surface carries explicit version identifiers, and the\n65\t  versioning scheme is documented.\n66\t- The deprecation policy is documented and mechanically enforced: use of\n67\t  deprecated surface produces the documented warning/behavior during the\n68\t  grace period.\n69\t- An automated upgrade-path test migrates a distribution from each of the\n70\t  last two Tech Preview releases to the GA release and passes.\n71\t- Every gap item in the ratified GA scope that falls in this epic's areas\n72\t  (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling) is either\n73\t  remediated or explicitly deferred with a recorded rationale accepted by\n74\t  stakeholders.\n75\t- All changes merge through a green Konflux build pipeline for the\n76\t  llama-stack midstream repo.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee —\n81\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the\n82\t  last two TP releases. This epic is the direct deliverer of HLR-2.\n83\t- Assessment-driven gap remediation (the actionable output of HLR-1) is\n84\t  bundled here: it edits the same API/quality surface of the same component\n85\t  and team as the stability work, so it is not a separately schedulable\n86\t  deliverable.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83473cf1cf19135a","agent_id":"a0e56b6a1c5c0aca8","session_id":"bc08d67b-4a0e-4de8-9000-b947c2646aca","uuid":"b273575c-bb77-4512-bf65-8c9ea5705a56","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:49:00.213Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-99cc94b22bc04e7d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
