on that belongs to this epic's deliverable,\n52\t  distinct from the platform-wide GA documentation uplift.\n53\t- Add/extend validation coverage for the integration in the TrustyAI\n54\t  operator and integration test suites.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The TrustyAI guardrails integration is available in GA Llama Stack\n59\t  distributions without any experimental opt-in flag.\n60\t- The integration is validated against the versioned GA API surface and\n61\t  across the published supported configuration matrix, and the validation\n62\t  passes as part of the integration test suite.\n63\t- Integration documentation is published describing configuration and\n64\t  supported topologies, marked as a supported (not experimental) capability.\n65\t- All changes merge through a green Konflux build pipeline for the TrustyAI\n66\t  midstream repo.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n71\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. This epic is\n72\t  the direct deliverer of HLR-4.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83473cf1cf19135a","agent_id":"a0e56b6a1c5c0aca8","session_id":"bc08d67b-4a0e-4de8-9000-b947c2646aca","uuid":"13d2ece8-ed62-4b24-894c-a0c2d1445564","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:49:04.254Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8607fb38d9fea732","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
